## Instructions

1. Read the feature plan and upstream handoff first.
2. Complete this stage with minimal changes and no unrelated refactoring; only change files required by the scope.
3. Write the handoff file using `.harness/templates/pipeline-handoff.md.template`; fill all required fields.
4. Do not run the gate command; the coordinator runs it after this stage finishes.
5. Do not create branches or run git push; Git/PR automation is handled by `script/harness-git.ps1`.
6. If scope deviation, missing dependency, or an Owner decision is needed, fill `escalations`; `blocking=true` pauses the pipeline.
7. Do not chat directly with other stage agents; pass results through handoff and artifacts only.
8. Record results, decisions, evidence, and remaining risks.
